# /etc/hunter/feeds — where `hunterctl update-signatures` downloads from.
#
#   <format> <name> <url> [<key>]
#
# format `sha256`: one SHA-256 per line (first field; `#` comments), every hash
#                  becomes `hash:<sha256>:<name>`.
# format `sigs`:   hunter's own signature lines (see /etc/hunter/signatures).
#
# With a <key> (a name from /etc/hunter/keys) the feed is signed: hunterctl
# also downloads <url>.sig, and the kernel installs the feed only if that
# signature is the key's, covers exactly these bytes, is for this feed name
# and is not older than the version installed. A signed feed is in `sigs`
# format. Without a key the feed is unsigned, taken on HTTPS alone, and
# refused altogether under `require-signed-feeds on`.
#
# Each feed lands in /etc/hunter/signatures.d/<name> (and <name>.sig), only
# if hunter accepted all of it; the last versions are kept in
# /var/lib/hunter/feeds/<name>/ for `hunterctl feed-rollback <name>`.
# To update every 6 hours with busybox crond:
#   0 */6 * * * /sbin/hunterctl update-signatures
#
# abuse.ch MalwareBazaar: SHA-256 of malware samples submitted in the last 48
# hours (free, no key needed for this export).
sha256 MalwareBazaar.Recent https://bazaar.abuse.ch/export/txt/sha256/recent/
#
# A signed feed, e.g. a mirror of the one above that you sign yourself
# (tools/hunterctl/hunter-feed-sign shows how):
# sigs MalwareBazaar.Signed https://example.org/hunter/recent mirror
